// aitypes pull the model + 441 xanims + behavior tree transitively (Avogadro/charred precedent);
// the .map actor spawners also reference them - belt-and-suspenders.
// archetype_acc_zod_robot_boss = OUR install-side GDT clone of the gold aitype with team=axis (the
// whole "make him hostile" trick - engine targeting is team-based; _acc_civil_protector.gsc header).
// NAMING IS LOAD-BEARING: spawner classname actor_spawner_<X> resolves to aitype archetype_<X> -
// the clone's first name "acc_zod_robot_boss" (no archetype_ prefix) made the linker/engine derive
// a nonexistent aitype from the .map spawner ("'spawner_acc_zod_robot_boss' is not a valid aitype")
// and the entity would be dropped at load. 2026-07-02.
aitype,archetype_ally_zod_robot_companion_ar
aitype,archetype_ally_zod_robot_companion_gold_ar
aitype,archetype_acc_zod_robot_boss
// spawner_ derived aitype = what SpawnActor("spawner_<X>", ...) resolves - MUST be zone-listed
// explicitly now that no BSP entity references it (the .map spawner crashed the load; the boss
// is SpawnActor'd directly in _acc_civil_protector::spawn_boss).
aitype,spawner_acc_zod_robot_boss
