// Charred Zombie base-horde reskin (Logical's Charred Zombie Pack): a custom
// aitype `archetype_charred_zombie` = stock factory-zombie behaviour/anims
// (zm_zombie.ai_bt + zm_factory_zombie anim tables) + charred character
// `c_zom_charred_zombie` (DLC3 sentinel body + DLC4 charred head) + matching
// `c_zom_charred_zombie_gib_def`. Character/gib materials pull transitively as
// MODEL dependencies, so they DODGE the brush-face shader trap (docs/29 §14) -
// same class of asset as the Brutus model, which builds fine here.
// Import: drag the pack's model_export/ + source_data/ into the Mod Tools root,
// then gdtdb /update (registers source_data/_charred_zombies.gdt).
// Whole-horde reskin = in Radiant, Remap the SINGLE base spawner
// (actor_spawner_zm_factory_zombie, origin -131.5 630.5 208) to the charred
// spawner class - do NOT duplicate it (a 2nd spawner => ~50/50 normal+charred mix).
// UNCOMMENT the line below AFTER the GDT is imported (else linker = "missing
// aitype"); the Radiant spawner placement also pulls the aitype as a BSP
// dependency, so this explicit line is belt-and-suspenders.
aitype,archetype_charred_zombie

// Stock "Giant" zombie BODY xmodel - used to SKIN the Glitch Stalker mini-boss so it stands out
// from the charred horde (_acc_boss_glitch.gsc SetModel). Stock base-game asset (t7_characters,
// gdtDB-registered, source bins on disk - NOT DLC/external); pulls its own materials transitively
// as a model dep (dodges the brush-face shader trap). Same 'base' skeleton + gib rig as charred,
// so the SetModel swap keeps anims/gibs intact. Verified via the glitch-base-skin workflow.
xmodel,c_zom_der_zombie_body1
// Stock "Giant" zombie HEAD xmodel - completes the FULL stock skin on the Glitch Stalker (the body
// above + this head; _acc_boss_glitch.gsc detaches the charred head and attaches this). Same stock
// der family + 'base' skeleton; links the same way as the body. (Use the gdtDB-registered name
// c_zom_der_zombie_head1 - the raw bin name c_zom_der_head_1 has NO xmodel GDT entry, so it fails
// to link. Same body/head naming family as c_zom_der_zombie_body1 above.)
xmodel,c_zom_der_zombie_head1
// TOXIC boss skins (user 2026-07-02): WetEgg SAT toxic bodies (heads included in the body models) -
// Glitch Stalker wears _1, Phantom wears _2 (script SetModel, so explicit lines; materials ride in
// transitively). EC-style model-only lift - external pack, see tools/external_assets_manifest.ps1
// "SAT Toxic Zombies" (marker source_data\acc_sat_toxic_zombies.gdt). The der body/head lines above
// stay: they remain the documented A/B fallback (acc_glitch_stock_skin / acc_phantom_stock_skin history).
xmodel,c_sat_zmb_zombie_toxic_1
xmodel,c_sat_zmb_zombie_toxic_2
// UNDERGROUND horde reskin (user 2026-07-03): Kingslayer Kyle's BOTD mob zombies (BO4
// Alcatraz prisoners; 3 bodies x 4 heads = the pack's own 12 combos, self-contained
// materials). Runtime SetModel+Attach by _acc_trench_skins on every zombie spawning below
// z=-36 (trench/under-rooms/abyss/Paradise) -> explicit lines (script-only refs); materials
// ride transitively. External pack, tools/external_assets_manifest.ps1 "BOTD Zombies".
// (Replaced Zeroy's 54i same day - its bodies render HEADLESS; 54i stays installed as fallback.)
xmodel,c_t8_zmb_mob_zombie_body1
xmodel,c_t8_zmb_mob_zombie_body2
xmodel,c_t8_zmb_mob_zombie_body3
xmodel,c_t8_zmb_mob_zombie_head1
xmodel,c_t8_zmb_mob_zombie_head2
xmodel,c_t8_zmb_mob_zombie_head3
xmodel,c_t8_zmb_mob_zombie_head4

// Custom ground-pickup world models (referenced ONLY by SetModel in script, so
// the linker needs these explicit lines - same reason as the Glitch Stalker
// models above). Stock assets, gdtDB-registered (verified via the dropped-item
// model workflow); materials ride in transitively (dodge the brush-face trap).
//   p7_fxanim_zm_stal_ray_gun_ball_mod = Data Shard drop (_acc_data_shards.gsc)
// Boss Cyberware items - one distinct model each (_acc_boss_items build_item_pool).
// 5 props packed here; item 4 "Repair Kit" uses a runtime-loaded powerup icon (no
// line needed). (zombie_zapper_handle + p6_power_lever were tried and FAILED to
// link - "xmodel missing", not in ZM-common fastfiles - so they were swapped out.)
//   nitrous_tank=Gas Tank, octobomb=Li'l Arnie, teddybear=Teddy Bear,
//   rocket_shield=Rocket Shield, monkey_bomb=Monkey Bomb
xmodel,p7_fxanim_zm_stal_ray_gun_ball_mod
xmodel,p7_zm_zod_nitrous_tank
xmodel,p7_fxanim_zm_zod_octobomb_mod
xmodel,p7_boots_safehouse_01
xmodel,zombietron_gold_brick
xmodel,wpn_t7_zmb_zod_rocket_shield_world
xmodel,wpn_t7_zmb_monkey_bomb_world
xmodel,wm_t6_five_seven
xmodel,wm_t6_olympia
// Wall-buy CHALK outlines (restored 2026-06-24): inline worldspawn meshes tokened
// mtl_t6_wpn_pistol_kard_wall_chalk / mtl_t6_wpn_shotty_olympia_wall_chalk / t7_zm_chalk_buy_frag.
// NO zone line needed - a mesh material is a FACE material, discovered from the brush token at
// cod2map time (same as the early t7_zm_chalk_buy_icr1 wall-buy that built fine, commit 0044a16).
// (The earlier "lit_emissive_transparent shader won't compile" claim was wrong: these are plain
// colorMap material.gdf assets, sources verified on disk in skye_t6_olympia / skye_t6_kap-40 GDTs.)
// Plaza Implant Bench prop: Cyber City white metal workbench (stock t7_props, on
// disk at model_export/t7_props/p7_cai_work_table_metal_set/). NOT in zm_levelcommon,
// so the linker compiles it from its GDT and packs it here (needs gdtdb-registered).
xmodel,p7_cai_work_table_metal_03_white
// Underground "Foundry" props (stock t7 props; same p7_cai_ family as the workbench
// above, so they compile from their GDTs + pack here). Glitch Altar base = interactive
// kiosk; Data Cache = cargo crate; Overclock terminal = ticket kiosk. Verified vs the
// build ERRORLOG (the oracle - see stock-pickup-model-safety).
xmodel,p7_cai_sign_inteactive_kiosk
xmodel,p7_cai_stacking_cargo_crate
xmodel,p7_cai_ticket_kiosk_theatre
// CW/BO6 Pack-a-Punch machine model (ALXS pack, user 2026-07-02, reworked same day):
// swapped at the PREFAB level - both PaP misc_prefabs point at
// _prefabs/acc/vending_weapon_upgrade_alxs.map, whose zbarrier entity board pieces are:
// board1 = the _off model (pre-power), board2/6 = the on model (their p7-rigged board
// anims blanked - rig mismatch); the sign flag + gun-mount tag boards stay stock.
// (Runtime SetModel on the zbarrier NO-OPS - boards render, not the base model.)
// The Paradise PaP clone (plain script_model) SetModels the on-model in _acc_pap_levels.gsc.
// GDT install-side: acc_alxs_pap.gdt.
xmodel,p9_fxanim_zm_gp_pap_xmodel
xmodel,p9_fxanim_zm_gp_pap_xmodel_off
// CW Miami night skybox (Nastian T9 Skyboxes pack, user 2026-07-02): worldspawn
// skyboxmodel -> skybox_t9_mp_miami (volume_sun ssi stays default_night - the pack
// ships no ssi). Sky is a NON-face asset -> explicit zone lines per docs/29. The
// xmodel reuses the stock t6_skybox dome mesh with a skinOverride to the HDR
// material below (sky_latlong_hdr). GDT install-side: acc_nastian_t9_skyboxes.gdt.
// 2026-07-02 sky experiments CLOSED: Miami (too light) then zm_silver_dark (user: "past sky was
// better") both rejected -> back to stock skybox_default_night (line 18 above) + default_night SSI.
// The Nastian pack stays installed (manifest, Required=$false) for future one-token experiments.
// NO material, line for the sky material (2026-07-02 build finding): an explicit
// material,mtl_skybox_t9_mp_miami line forces the STANDALONE techset compile, which fails on
// this install (8x "techsetdef_sky_latlong_hdr.hlsl Shader preprocessor error" + GetTechnique
// (unlit) failed - the docs/29 SS14 trap, confirmed present even on the pristine 2026-07-01
// tools reinstall). The material rides in TRANSITIVELY as an xmodel dep instead (docs/56 rule -
// same path every custom model material here ships through). If the sky renders black/missing
// in game, the latlong-HDR sky class is unshippable on this install -> revert worldspawn to
// skybox_default_night (full bake).
// WW2 circuit-breaker power-switch BODY (Fanatic pack, user 2026-07-02; prefab reworked
// same day): the map's power_switch misc_prefab points at our clone prefab
// _prefabs/acc/power_switch_ww2.map - stock prefab with the body misc_model swapped to
// this xmodel (+ local yaw 270 so the face points at the use trigger) and the stock
// p7 handle script_model DELETED (user request; stock _zm_power::electric_switch guards
// every master_switch use with isdefined -> deletion-safe: power flips fine, no handle
// flip anim/sound, spark FX skipped by the same guard). Trigger + fx struct unchanged.
// Model-only lift: the pack's own GSC/sounds/anims system is deliberately NOT installed.
// GDT install-side: source_data\fanatic\ww2\ww2_power_switch.gdt.
xmodel,ww2_circuit_breaker
// T7 prop-pack PILOT decor (MidgetBlaster "T7 Assets V2.7", user 2026-07-02): two static
// props spawned in the Exchange transfer-vault room by _acc_atmosphere::spawn_exchange_props
// (Moon server rack + crucible holo monitor). Install-side slice: source_data\
// acc_t7_props_pilot.gdt + model_export\_midgetblaster\props\** (PNG baseImages - the
// PNG-pipeline pilot). Some carved materials reference stock $-builtin / stock-named
// images (not re-defined) - expect them to resolve from stock; errorlog is the oracle.
xmodel,p7_zm_moo_server_comm_02
xmodel,p7_cru_monitor_holo_screen_01
// Cymbal Monkey (cymbal_monkey_zm) + Octobomb / Li'l Arnie (octobomb_zm) are
// granted by boss items. Both weapon DEFS already ship in zm_levelcommon (every
// usermap loads it at runtime - assetlist lines 6175 + 6225), so we do NOT add a
// `weapon,<name>_zm` line here: that forces a re-pack from a GDT source that ISN'T
// on disk and errors "Unable to load weapon". Inclusion is done purely via CSV rows
// in gamedata/weapons/zm/zm_levelcommon_weapons.csv (is_weapon_included -> true);
// GetWeapon("octobomb"/"cymbal_monkey") then resolves from zm_levelcommon. (Earlier
// build error was self-inflicted by the redundant weapon, lines - removed.)

// LUI client pipeline foundation (server module + client mirror + Lua overlay).
// docs/28_lui_pipeline.md. The .lua is a rawfile (copied verbatim, parsed by the
// game's Lua VM at runtime - a Lua syntax error shows at load, NOT at link).
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_lui.gsc
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_lui.csc
// Client half of the perk/PaP power-on glow (REGISTER_SYSTEM mirror + PlayFX render).
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_perk_lights.csc
// Client half of the Phantom holographic glow aura (accPhantomAura clientfield -> PlayFXOnTag).
scriptparsetree,scripts/zm/zm_abandoned_cyber_city/_acc_boss_phantom.csc
rawfile,ui/uieditor/menus/hud/acc_hud.lua

